when you need your blade sharpened the  best thing to do is have a couple of  blades on hand so that you can take one  off and then put on the new blade and  while that way can be used for another  eight to ten to twelve hours of use then  you take the blade you took off to the  local hardware store and most of the  local hardware store should be able to  put a nice edge on you and it's  important having a sharp blade not only  keeps the plants healthy but it costs  you less and fuel in the long run so the  first thing I like to do is grab a piece  of cardboard is something lay down on no  matter how much you try to clean your  concrete pad it's always going to be  dirty and if that's a concern for you  this makes a nice surface to lay down on  one thing i like to keep with me when  i'm changing blades and what I'm taking  them off is a welding glove you can pick  these up at your local hardware store a  large rag works well I like a glove  because I can actually hold on to the  blade there's no chance of its slipping  out of my hand when you're taking a  blade off if you're not holding on to it  it's going to want to turn on you you  never want to be use a socket to take a  blade off if you're not holding on to it  when you're laying on your back trying  to take a blade off sometimes  counterclockwise and clockwise becomes  confusing so what I do is before I use  my tool I'll make sure that it's  loosening up or tightening down  depending on what I'm doing and I'll set  it before hand so when I crawl  underneath the machine I'm already set  up to do it okay  now when you take them out what I like  to do is just mark it right top on it  whatever helps you put that blade back  in the same way I like to use the center  block is something to hold the top of  the lower down this way you can access  the blade safely just remember with  these small rotary mowers you don't want  to leave them tip back for very long gas  and oil can move on you and they'll  start spilling out remove your blade  move your tools to the side and lift up  your cinder block and set the mower back  down until you're ready to put your  blade back on
 

